# Phase Balance Summary

| Phase | Focus | Main work packages |
|-------|--------|---------------------|
| **1** | Operational pipeline (AWS) | Contract, Ingestion, SQS, Aggregator, DynamoDB, API Gateway, AWS Terraform, basic observability, CI |
| **2** | Cross-cloud and analytics | Forwarder, Pub/Sub, Analytics, BigQuery, GCP Terraform, GCP observability, event schema alignment, CI for GCP |
| **3** | Event backbone and production | Kafka/MSK, schema registry (opt.), migration, replay, Grafana, alerting, E2E tests, load/runbooks, OIDC/security |

Each phase delivers a **shippable slice**: Phase 1 = operational system on AWS; Phase 2 = multi-cloud analytics; Phase 3 = production-grade event backbone and observability. Work is spread across infra, application, observability, and quality in all three phases so that no single phase is disproportionately large or small.

